{"id":"m68807:problem:fs-idm9714880","rulings":["functional-group"],"maxOps":6,"en":"(b) Aspirin was discovered as a result of efforts to produce a derivative of salicylic acid that would not be irritating to the stomach lining. Aspirin is acetylsalicylic acid, CH[[sub:3]]CO[[sub:2]]C[[sub:6]]H[[sub:4]]CO[[sub:2]]H. The −CO[[sub:2]]H functional group is still present, but its acidity is reduced, [[i:K]][[sub:a]] = 3.0 [[MATH:35]] 10[[sup:−4]]. What is the pH of a solution of aspirin with the same concentration as a saturated solution of salicylic acid (See Part a).","is":"(b) Aspirín var uppgötvað í tilraunum til að framleiða afleiðu salisýlsýru sem myndi ekki erta magaslímhúðina. Aspirín er asetýlsalisýlsýra, CH[[sub:3]]CO[[sub:2]]C[[sub:6]]H[[sub:4]]CO[[sub:2]]H. Virki flokkurinn –CO[[sub:2]]H er enn til staðar, en sýrustig hans er minna, [[i:K]][[sub:a]] = 3,0 [[MATH:35]] 10[[sup:−4]]. Hvert er pH aspirínlausnar með sama styrk og mettuð lausn af salisýlsýru (sjá a-lið)?"},
